Spec: Pen Tool

Purpose:
  Create Bézier paths by placing anchor points with optional control handles.

Owns:
  ./pen.ts
  ./pen.test.ts

Must:
  Click places a corner node (straight segment).
  Click+drag places a smooth node (curved segment with tangent handles).
  Shift constrains new segments to 45° increments.
  Clicking the first node closes the path.
  Enter or Escape finishes as an open path.
  Preview line shows from last node to cursor during drawing.
  Snap to existing endpoints/midpoints when enabled.
  Created path is pushed to store via CreateShapeCommand.

Must not:
  Modify existing shapes.
  Create zero-length paths (discard if only one node placed).
  Leave the path in an uncommitted state after tool switch.

Depends on:
  @BaseTool
  @PathShape
  @PathNode
  @CreateShapeCommand
  @SnapManager

Scenario: draw closed triangle
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user clicks at 3 positions and clicks the first node to close
  Then a closed PathShape with 3 corner nodes exists in the store
  And it is the selected shape

Scenario: draw open path with Enter
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user clicks at 3 positions and presses Enter
  Then an open PathShape with 3 nodes exists in the store

Scenario: draw open path with Escape
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user clicks at 2 positions and presses Escape
  Then an open PathShape with 2 nodes exists in the store

Scenario: click+drag creates smooth node
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user click+drags at a position
  Then the placed node has type 'smooth' with non-zero control handles

Scenario: discard single-node path
  Given the Pen tool is active
  When the user clicks once and presses Escape
  Then no shape is created (single-point paths are discarded)

Scenario: shift constrains to 45 degrees
  Given the Pen tool is active and one node has been placed
  When the user holds Shift and clicks at an angle near 30 degrees
  Then the segment snaps to the nearest 45-degree increment (0 or 45)

Scenario: preview line follows cursor
  Given the Pen tool is active and one node is placed
  When the user moves the cursor
  Then a preview line is visible from the last node to the cursor position

Scenario: undo removes last placed node
  Given the Pen tool is active and 3 nodes have been placed
  When the user presses Ctrl+Z
  Then the path under construction has 2 nodes

Tasks:
  [x] Click to place corner nodes.
  [x] Click+drag for smooth nodes.
  [x] Close path by clicking first node.
  [x] Finish open path with Enter/Escape.
  [x] Preview line rendering.
  [x] Shift constraint for 45° angles.
  [x] Integration with snap system.
